_design:
Content is deliberately mixed rather than uniform tutoring prose, because the failure modes differ by input type and a set of only well-formed sentences hides most of them:
  - numbers, units and abbreviations (C5-T1, 15 to 90 degrees) — the classic TTS normalisation failure;
  - long multi-clause sentences — where prosody and breath placement break down;
  - short fragments — where models trained on full sentences clip or rush;
  - anatomical Latin inside Tamil and Sinhala — the actual code-switch case this system exists to handle, and the one no single-language TTS is trained for.
